## 4. Naming rationale

- **`runUserDataValidationRules`** — "run the rules" signals this is the engine that executes all the checks, as distinct from `validateUserData`, which is the stable public entry point. Alternatives: `applyValidationRules`, `executeUserDataValidation`.
- **Parameters**: `userData` and `options` are passed through unchanged, since every one of the 9 concerns you listed depends on one or both of them (`options.isRegistration`, `options.checkExisting`, `options.customValidations`).

**Worth flagging:** because this extraction pulls in *all* the logic at once, you don't get the usual benefits of decomposition (independent testability, one-concern-per-function, easier scanning) — `runUserDataValidationRules` is just as long and multi-purpose as the original. If the goal is actually improving readability/testability rather than adding a wrapper seam, the split I did in the earlier message (one function per concern — `validateUsername`, `validatePassword`, `validateEmail`, etc.) gets you there; this single-function extraction is better suited to a narrower goal like keeping `validateUserData`'s signature stable while renaming/relocating the implementation.












Prompt 3: Conditional Logic Simplification
## 1. Logical paths through the conditionals

The function branches on:

- **Top-level fork**: `isRegistration` → registration required-fields + username + password rules, **or else** → profile required-fields rules
- **Nested branches** within each section: username (length-short / length-long / bad-chars / taken), password (short / no-uppercase / no-lowercase / no-number / no-special), email (empty+registration / empty+not-registration / bad-format / taken), date-of-birth (invalid-date / future / too-young / too-old), address (not-an-object / missing-sub-fields / bad-postal-code-per-country), phone (bad-format), custom (per-validator pass/fail)

Each of these is really the same shape: **"if this field is present and doesn't satisfy some predicate, add this error."** That repeated shape is what makes Strategy a good fit.

## 2 & 3. Extracting branches + the pattern

Rather than one big if/else-if chain deciding which checks to run, model each validation as a **rule object**: `{ appliesTo(userData, options), check(userData, options) }`. The main function stops containing any conditional logic about *which* checks to run — it just runs the applicable rules in a loop. This is the **Strategy pattern**: each rule is an interchangeable "validation strategy," selected by its own `appliesTo` predicate instead of a hardcoded if-chain.

```javascript
const RULES = [
  {
    name: 'requiredRegistrationFields',
    appliesTo: (data, opts) => opts.isRegistration,
    check: (data) => {
      const errors = [];
      for (const field of ['username', 'email', 'password', 'confirmPassword']) {
        if (!data[field] || data[field].trim() === '') errors.push(`${field} is required for registration`);
      }
      return errors;
    }
  },
  {
    name: 'requiredProfileFields',
    appliesTo: (data, opts) => !opts.isRegistration,
    check: (data) => {
      const errors = [];
      for (const field of ['firstName', 'lastName', 'dateOfBirth', 'address']) {
        if (data[field] !== undefined && data[field].trim() === '') errors.push(`${field} cannot be empty if provided`);
      }
      return errors;
    }
  },
  {
    name: 'username',
    appliesTo: (data, opts) => opts.isRegistration && !!data.username,
    check: (data, opts) => {
      const { username } = data;
      if (username.length < 3) return ['Username must be at least 3 characters long'];
      if (username.length > 20) return ['Username must be at most 20 characters long'];
      if (!/^[a-zA-Z0-9_]+$/.test(username)) return ['Username can only contain letters, numbers, and underscores'];
      if (opts.checkExisting?.usernameExists(username)) return ['Username is already taken'];
      return [];
    }
  },
  {
    name: 'password',
    appliesTo: (data, opts) => opts.isRegistration,
    check: (data) => {
      const { password, confirmPassword } = data;
      const errors = [];
      if (password) {
        if (password.length < 8) errors.push('Password must be at least 8 characters long');
        else if (!/[A-Z]/.test(password)) errors.push('Password must contain at least one uppercase letter');
        else if (!/[a-z]/.test(password)) errors.push('Password must contain at least one lowercase letter');
        else if (!/[0-9]/.test(password)) errors.push('Password must contain at least one number');
        else if (!/[^A-Za-z0-9]/.test(password)) errors.push('Password must contain at least one special character');
      }
      if (confirmPassword !== password) errors.push('Password and confirmation do not match');
      return errors;
    }
  },
  {
    name: 'email',
    appliesTo: (data) => data.email !== undefined,
    check: (data, opts) => {
      const { email } = data;
      if (email.trim() === '') return opts.isRegistration ? ['Email is required'] : [];
      if (!/^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/.test(email)) return ['Email format is invalid'];
      if (opts.checkExisting?.emailExists(email)) return ['Email is already registered'];
      return [];
    }
  },
  {
    name: 'dateOfBirth',
    appliesTo: (data) => !!data.dateOfBirth,
    check: (data) => {
      const dob = new Date(data.dateOfBirth);
      if (isNaN(dob.getTime())) return ['Date of birth is not a valid date'];
      const now = new Date();
      const minAgeDate = new Date(now.getFullYear() - 13, now.getMonth(), now.getDate());
      const maxAgeDate = new Date(now.getFullYear() - 120, now.getMonth(), now.getDate());
      if (dob > now) return ['Date of birth cannot be in the future'];
      if (dob > minAgeDate) return ['You must be at least 13 years old'];
      if (dob < maxAgeDate) return ['Invalid date of birth (age > 120 years)'];
      return [];
    }
  },
  {
    name: 'address',
    appliesTo: (data) => !!data.address,
    check: (data) => {
      const { address } = data;
      if (typeof address !== 'object') return ['Address must be an object with required fields'];
      const errors = [];
      for (const field of ['street', 'city', 'zip', 'country']) {
        if (!address[field] || address[field].trim() === '') errors.push(`Address ${field} is required`);
      }
      const postalRegex = { US: /^\d{5}(-\d{4})?$/, CA: /^[A-Za-z]\d[A-Za-z] \d[A-Za-z]\d$/, UK: /^[A-Z]{1,2}\d[A-Z\d]? \d[A-Z]{2}$/ };
      const postalError = { US: 'Invalid US ZIP code format', CA: 'Invalid Canadian postal code format', UK: 'Invalid UK postal code format' };
      if (address.zip && address.country && postalRegex[address.country] && !postalRegex[address.country].test(address.zip)) {
        errors.push(postalError[address.country]);
      }
      return errors;
    }
  },
  {
    name: 'phone',
    appliesTo: (data) => !!data.phone,
    check: (data) => (/^\+?[\d\s\-()]{10,15}$/.test(data.phone) ? [] : ['Phone number format is invalid'])
  },
  {
    name: 'customValidations',
    appliesTo: (data, opts) => !!opts.customValidations,
    check: (data, opts) => {
      const errors = [];
      for (const { field, validator, message } of opts.customValidations) {
        if (data[field] !== undefined && !validator(data[field], data)) {
          errors.push(message || `Invalid value for ${field}`);
        }
      }
      return errors;
    }
  }
];
